<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to sell 0.3-pct diesel for Sep 5-30.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to sell 0.3-pct diesel for Sep 5-30.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to sell 225,000-250,000 barrels of 0.3 percent sulphur diesel for September 5-30 lifting, free-on-board Kaohsiung, a CPC source said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on August 11 and bids will be valid for three days.</p>
<p>CPC sold two cargoes in its last tender for August 15-20 and August 25-29 liftings at around $20.30-$20.50 per barrel, fob basis, to a Swiss trader and a US major.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3084)</p>
